   183	## 5. Server-to-Client Messages
   184	
   185	### 5.1 connected
   186	
   187	Sent exactly once after a successful handshake. See Section 2.3.
   188	
   189	| Field            | Type     | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |
   190	| ---------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
   375	- `stream_end` follows every stream even after an error: a failed run sends its `error` frame first and `stream_end` last.
   376	- An `error` frame does not by itself end a stream. It is advisory: it may concern the run in flight or an unrelated frame, such as a malformed `ping`.
   377	- The client SHOULD use this message to clear any "processing" or "loading" indicators.
   378	- The client MUST treat a run as complete only at `stream_end` or when the socket closes. Unparseable JSON is the one frame answered with `INVALID_FORMAT` and no `stream_end`, because the server cannot tell what it was meant to be; for it the client falls back on the socket closing.
